; Host - which target this compiler binary itself runs on.
; See `Host.darwin-aarch64.ax` for why this is a compile-time constant
; selected by module resolution rather than a runtime query.
;
; This file exists so that compiling the compiler FOR windows-aarch64
; resolves `Host` at all, as `Host.windows-x86_64.ax` does for the
; other Windows architecture. No compiler binary has yet run on
; Windows: hosting the compiler there is a later phase of the Windows
; track.
(pub :: hostTarget String)
(pub fn (hostTarget)
  "windows-aarch64")
